WEBVTT

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:09.710
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the 23rd of March. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the Teams mime again?</v>

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:17.750
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, you're there. Sorry, only just sat down. Traffic on the ring road was absolutely solid.</v>

00:00:18.929 --> 00:00:24.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Saw that coming in. Whose new car's in the car park, then? Very shiny for this place.</v>

00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:31.230
<v Hannah Price>Give it a day. It'll be the same colour as all the others.</v>

00:00:32.719 --> 00:00:38.320
<v Sarah Okafor>Ha. Also, there's a birthday cake in the office. Before anyone asks, no, it's not mine.</v>

00:00:39.109 --> 00:00:41.560
<v Jamie Brennan>That's the important operational update covered, then.</v>

00:00:42.259 --> 00:00:46.460
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, enough. Finished stuff first, then what's actually going on the list.</v>

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:53.700
<v Jamie Brennan>I tested the Palletiser yesterday and it's all fine now. That's done, not another job for today.</v>

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.950
<v Aisha Begum>Was that with it cycling properly, rather than just powered up?</v>

00:01:01.229 --> 00:01:04.379
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, cycling. All fine. Nothing outstanding from that test.</v>

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:12.760
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same sort of update from me: tested the gas turbine two yesterday and it's all fine now.</v>

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:19.019
<v Grace Liu>And I finished the repair on the GT2 Number 2 Bearing last night. That one's complete.</v>

00:01:19.769 --> 00:01:25.719
<v Tomasz Nowak>I noticed the number two bearing was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:31.030
<v Hannah Price>Settled back down, yeah? You're not raising another repair there?</v>

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:37.709
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, no. Just saying what I saw. It settled down; not putting another job in.</v>

00:01:39.609 --> 00:01:44.510
<v Grace Liu>Other thing: the shutdown on the boiler is cancelled now, production need it running.</v>

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.209
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, cancelled. That stays off the work list, then.</v>

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:55.969
<v Aisha Begum>And we're still waiting on parts for the line one HPU. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:01.859
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, the parts-dependent work's blocked. Not pretending that's available to do today.</v>

00:02:03.959 --> 00:02:06.060
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. Same position as before, unfortunately.</v>

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:12.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie Brennan, can you investigate the pressure drop on the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit on the 3rd?</v>

00:02:13.879 --> 00:02:19.129
<v Jamie Brennan>Investigate, rather than take on the repair that's waiting for parts? Just keeping those separate.</v>

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:28.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, just investigate the pressure drop on the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit on the 3rd. Not assigning the blocked repair.</v>

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:36.599
<v Jamie Brennan>Okay, agreed. I'll investigate the pressure drop on the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit on the 3rd.</v>

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:43.229
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, that distinction matters. Otherwise it reads like the parts have magically appeared.</v>

00:02:44.689 --> 00:02:50.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Olu, can you swap the filter on the compressor one today? That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:02:51.939 --> 00:02:57.539
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, I'll swap the filter on the compressor one today, straight away. Understood on safety critical.</v>

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:02.460
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, that's not one to bury underneath the routine stuff.</v>

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.449
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, understood. Immediate one for me.</v>

00:03:05.969 --> 00:03:13.319
<v Aisha Begum>While we're on the compressor one, it still needs someone to take vibration readings. Low priority, though, separate from the filter.</v>

00:03:13.879 --> 00:03:18.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone actually taking the vibration readings, or is that still without a name?</v>

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:23.229
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I'm taking the filter, not the readings. Don't put both against me.</v>

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:29.099
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, vibration readings on the compressor one stay unassigned. Low priority, no owner.</v>

00:03:29.719 --> 00:03:36.719
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll replace the seals on the water booster first thing tomorrow. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:38.389 --> 00:03:43.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tomasz. Water booster seals, first thing tomorrow, first job because it's holding production up.</v>

00:03:45.979 --> 00:03:48.080
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, that's mine. First thing tomorrow.</v>

00:03:50.259 --> 00:03:55.509
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, talking over you—first tomorrow, not shifting the safety-critical filter out of the way today?</v>

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:00.599
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Different timing. Today's filter is straight away; seals first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:04:02.189 --> 00:04:07.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you do a site visit at the water works with the contractor Monday?</v>

00:04:07.949 --> 00:04:10.750
<v Jamie Brennan>Monday as in today, yeah? Not next week?</v>

00:04:11.979 --> 00:04:16.529
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, today, Monday. The site visit at the water works with the contractor.</v>

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:23.410
<v Jamie Brennan>Right, accepted. I'll do a site visit at the water works with the contractor Monday.</v>

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.819
<v Aisha Begum>Out of stores and into the fresh air. Luxury.</v>

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.439
<v Jamie Brennan>Your definition of luxury and mine are miles apart.</v>

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:41.410
<v Hannah Price>There's also ordering spare parts for the main conveyor. That needs doing tomorrow at 9:30, but there's no name against it.</v>

00:04:43.379 --> 00:04:47.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Anyone able to take ordering those spare parts for the main conveyor?</v>

00:04:50.339 --> 00:04:55.240
<v Jamie Brennan>I can't take that one. Don't assume it's mine just because it says parts.</v>

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:59.819
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'm not taking it either. Just to be clear.</v>

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:06.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, nobody's taken it. Order spare parts for the main conveyor, tomorrow at 9:30, still unassigned.</v>

00:05:07.959 --> 00:05:11.459
<v Aisha Begum>So that's outstanding, not an order that's already gone through?</v>

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.829
<v Hannah Price>Correct, outstanding. No order placed and no owner agreed.</v>

00:05:18.269 --> 00:05:28.069
<v Sarah Okafor>On the planning side, I'll schedule downtime for the line three with production by Wednesday. That's in the 'whenever you get a chance' category, not an urgent one.</v>

00:05:29.319 --> 00:05:34.569
<v Aisha Begum>Okay, Sarah. Whenever you get a chance, but still by Wednesday for getting it scheduled?</v>

00:05:35.139 --> 00:05:39.339
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, exactly. I'll have it scheduled by Wednesday. Lower urgency, same deadline.</v>

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:43.019
<v Hannah Price>And the shift handover report going round—is that covered?</v>

00:05:45.209 --> 00:05:48.709
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round by Wednesday.</v>

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.439
<v Jamie Brennan>Cheers, Saz. That's clear.</v>

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:58.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. And the two things without names really are without names. Silence isn't somebody volunteering.</v>

00:06:00.899 --> 00:06:06.850
<v Grace Liu>Fine by me. And just keeping the cancelled boiler shutdown separate from all that. It's not pending.</v>

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:12.540
<v Aisha Begum>Same with the parts wait I mentioned: blocked work, not a fresh commitment.</v>

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:19.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. That's the distinction. Anything else that's just a correction to what we've said?</v>

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:23.629
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No correction. Only concern is whether that cake survives this call.</v>

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:29.180
<v Hannah Price>On Teams? You can practically hear people cutting it in the background.</v>

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:31.839
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we're done. Thanks, everyone.</v>
